{"id": "toolu_01MzA1VBuXxoaSVVBruPPThb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"code": "open('notes.md','a').write(\"\"\"\n- Exp A result (passes 8-9, featsA.npz = C7..C11', M7..M11' of layer6-tapped model): tap works locally (C7' 94.9 vs base 92.5)\n  but washes out by L11 (C11'+M11' concat 96.7 = no gain). token mean feats change ~4-5%. [C7',M11'] only 96.9; M6+M11' 97.5.\n- Idea: readout at layer R (exact readout design) + layers R+1..11 identity (Wo=0,bo=0,LN g=1 b=0, W2=0,b2=0) -> can use [C_R, M_R] for any R, or tap at k with readout at R=k+1..k+2.\n- CURRENT SAVED EDITS: layer11 readout (base C11+M11) + layer6 Wq tap (tap is harmless but useless -> should drop or rebuild readout on featsA). \n\"\"\")\nF=np.load('feats.npz'); y=F['y']; folds=np.load('folds.npy'); A=dict(np.load('featsA.npz'))\ndef stdz(X,tr): mu=X[tr].mean(0); sd=X[tr].std(0)+1e-6; return (X-mu)/sd\ndef cv(featfn, lam):\n    accs=[]\n    for f in range(5):\n        tr=folds!=f; te=~tr\n        Z=featfn(tr); mu=Z[tr].mean(0); Zc=Z-mu\n        Y=np.eye(8)[y[tr]]-1/8\n        K=Zc@Zc[tr].T; a=np.linalg.solve(K[tr]+lam*np.eye(tr.sum()),Y); pr=K[te]@a\n        accs.append((np.argmax(pr,1)==y[te]).mean())\n    return round(np.mean(accs),4)\nfor R in [4,5,6,7,8,9,10,11]:\n    fn=lambda tr: np.concatenate([0.85*stdz(F[f'C{R}'],tr),stdz(F[f'M{R}'],tr)],1)\n    print('base [C%d,M%d]'%(R,R),[cv(fn,l) for l in [100,200,300,500]])\nfor R in [7,8]:\n    fn=lambda tr: np.concatenate([0.85*stdz(A[f'C{R}'],tr),stdz(A[f'M{R}'],tr)],1)\n    print(\"tapped [C%d',M%d']\"%(R,R),[cv(fn,l) for l in [100,200,300,500]])"}, "name": "run_python", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}
